NISHIKAWA, TAKAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIKAWA TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA TATSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIKAWA, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMODA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method including a step of forming a first region (24) on which the material of a member of a ferroelectric capacitor section is easily deposited and a second region (26) on which the material for forming the ferroelectric capacitor section is less easily deposited than the first region (24), in the surface of a substrate (10) on which a transistor is formed, and a step of supplying materials to the substrate (10), and forming a first electrode (32), a ferroelectric film (34), and a second electrode (36) in the first region (24).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un procédé consistant à former une première région (24) sur laquelle il est facile de déposer le matériau d'un élément d'une section à effet de condensateur ferroélectrique et une seconde région (26) sur laquelle il est moins facile de déposer le matériau destiné à la formation de la section à effet de condensateur ferroélectrique, que cela ne l'est sur la première région (24), les deux régions étant disposées à la surface d'un substrat (10) sur lequel un transistor est formé. Ledit procédé consiste à amener les matériaux sur le substrat (10) et à former une première électrode (32), un film ferroélectrique (34) et une seconde électrode (36) dans la première région (24).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>